    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0243" n="223" xml:id="pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">495A.119/6–2850: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Certain Diplomatic Missions
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d143-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">plain</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-28T20:00:00-04:00">June 28, 1950—8 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In order to implement UN SC Resolution of June 27 requesting member governments
                    refrain from giving aid North Korea, US instituted complete embargo of exports
                    to North Korea effective 4 p. m. June 28, 1950. Inform Government to which
                        accredited.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d143-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d143-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d143-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to all diplomatic missions except Bucharest, Budapest, Moscow, Prague.
                    Sofia, and Warsaw.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d143-f2" n="2" xml:id="d143-f2-content">
                <p>For documentation on this subject, see <ref target="frus1950v06#pg_256">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, pp. 256</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
